# Component overgroups in Section 15.3

This is the assembly boundary for Aschbacher--Smith 15.3.33--45 (combined
manuscript of 1 March 2004, printed pp.1134--1140).

`LocalSetup` proves the exact hypotheses required to apply 1.1.5 in
15.3.33(2). `Uniqueness` proves the minimal-overgroup reduction and the
deduction of all three clauses of 15.3.45 for both definite planes.
`Fusion` establishes the distinct-conjugate condition and the corrected
I.6.2 application in 15.3.38.
The component classification and exclusions 15.3.34--43, including the
diagonal-outer L₃(4) transfer argument, are still needed to discharge
the uniqueness input. No source uniqueness theorem is asserted here
until those exclusions have been assembled.
-/
